    "introductoryText": "### Salesforce REST OAuth\n\nThe easiest way to use this connector is **Simple - Load object**: choose a familiar Salesforce object such as Accounts, Contacts or Opportunities. The block automatically discovers every field available to the OAuth Run As user and loads the records into Omniscope. You do not need to know Salesforce field API names or write SOQL.\n\n#### Salesforce setup\n1. In Salesforce Setup, create/configure an **External Client App** with OAuth enabled and the **Manage user data via APIs (`api`)** scope.\n2. Enable the **Client Credentials Flow** and configure its **Run As** user in the app policies. That user's Salesforce permissions determine which objects and fields this block can read.\n3. Copy the app **Consumer Key** and **Consumer Secret** into the OAuth options below.\n4. Use your Salesforce **My Domain URL**, e.g. `https://your-company.my.salesforce.com`.\n\n#### Load modes\n- **Simple - Load object (recommended):** choose a common Salesforce object; all available fields are discovered and selected automatically.\n- **Query Builder:** for advanced users who want to specify an object, fields, WHERE and ORDER BY.\n- **Custom SOQL:** for expert Salesforce users who want full SOQL control.\n\nThe optional schema actions can still list every object available to the authenticated user or describe an object's fields. Records are loaded through the synchronous REST Query API with automatic pagination.",
